  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.8 - Accurate CUDA math without the prefill cost: on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.21 the flash-prefill softmax runs XMath.Exp2 (one ex2) and the dequant f16 scales are converted from bits, so CUDA prefill is 293 tok/s short / 7,690 long (qwen3:1.7b Q8_0, RTX 4070) with or without the CUDA toolkit, against 232 / 7,435 in 5.8.7 on a toolkit machine. ML hot loops use float.MultiplyAddEstimate, so an app that builds its own Context no longer needs EnableFloatingPointContraction for speed. SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.19-5.4.21 CUDA fixes (nested-loop miscompile, warp-uniform branch at O2), -0 constants and locale-independent codegen on the browser backends. Release sweep 7,654 passed, 0 failed. Full notes: CHANGELOG.md.",
